// c-error-op-04: `<`/`>`/`<=`/`>=` accept references and compare their
// bind ids. Parallel compile mints those ids from a global counter in
// thread order, so a program with no input prints a different value from
// run to run.
//
// command (run it ten times):
//   graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/c-error-op-04.gx
//   graphix-fuzz run design/review-2026-10-05/repro/c-error-op-04.gx
//
// expected: the same answer on every run. CLAUDE.md says a reference is not
// a number (a cast of one is refused), and design/parallel_compile.md says
// "anything that iterates by id must not change output". So the check
// should refuse an ordering comparison over a type that can hold a
// reference, as it refuses the cast.
//
// observed: `--check` exits 0. Two sets of ten runs printed `false` 7 and
// 3 times, `true` the rest (`--no-fusion` flips too). With
// RAYON_NUM_THREADS=1 every run prints `true`. Nothing fuses
// (`graphix-fuzz run`: fused=0), yet its sessions disagree within one run:
//   Interp: false, Jit: true, Interp/nocache: false, Interp/cold: true
// `graphix-fuzz check` reported DIVERGENCE in 2 of 12 runs, labelled
// "image bug: writing the program image changed the program". A generic
// `|a, b| a < b` called with references, `array::sort` over references and
// a Map keyed by references flip in the same way.
let mk = |x: i64| {
    let v = x;
    &v
};
let r1 = mk(5);
let r2 = mk(6);
let out = r1 < r2;
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0));
out
